tinacloud-org(1) -- Interact with TinaCloud organisations
==========================================================

## SYNOPSIS

`tinacloud org` <command>

## DESCRIPTION

View organisations available to the signed-in TinaCloud user and rank their users by activity count.

## COMMANDS

  * `list`:
    List organisations.

  * `leaderboard`:
    Rank organisation users by activity count. The date range defaults to the
    first day of the current month through today.

    Use `--from` and `--to` together to set dates in YYYY-MM-DD format, `--all` to
    include users with zero activity, `--org-id` to select an organisation,
    `--tina-dir` to set the path to the tina folder, and `--json` for JSON output.

    Use `--period` to select `this-month`, `last-month`, `3-months`, or
    `12-months`. The three- and twelve-month periods include the current month
    through today. `last-month` covers the previous calendar month. `--period`
    cannot be combined with `--from` or `--to`.

## EXAMPLES

List the organisations available to the signed-in account:

	$ tinacloud org list

Print the result as JSON:

	$ tinacloud org list --json

Show the leaderboard, including users with zero activity:

	$ tinacloud org leaderboard --all

Show the leaderboard for the previous calendar month:

	$ tinacloud org leaderboard --period last-month

